    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **45 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp31Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required returning `checkDigit` \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`. I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema, right after `customerCode`. `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time, so this surfaces the field in the API response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(checkDigit(owner))\")` and a `checkDigit(Owner)` default method that computes the Luhn check digit over the digits of `customerCode`. It follows the existing derived-field pattern (like `membershipNumber`) and returns `null` when `customerCode` is absent so owners without a code map cleanly.\n\nThe Luhn implementation mirrors the algorithm the acceptance test uses (`AcceptanceBase.luhn`): scan right-to-left, double every second digit starting from the rightmost, subtract 9 if >9, then `(10 - sum % 10) % 10`. `Cp31Tests` recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit \u2014 it passes.",
